+# Vet Pagination Links Carry the Specialty as Link-Expression Parameters
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VET-003` narrows the veterinarian directory to one specialty, and a narrowed page's pagination links must keep the narrowing. The name arrives as a request parameter, so callers control its text.
+
+The five pagination links in `vets/vetList.html` built their `href` by Thymeleaf expression preprocessing — `@{'/vets.html?page=__${i}__'}`. Preprocessing splices the value into the expression before the expression is parsed, and applies no URL encoding.
+
+Two facts about Thymeleaf link expressions decide the shape. A parameter value is URL-encoded. A `null` parameter value renders as an empty `specialty=` rather than being omitted.
+
+The second fact was assumed the other way when this slice was first triaged, and building the links disproved it.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Extend the preprocessing form to the specialty.** Rejected: caller text would reach the expression parser, which is expression injection, and preprocessing skips URL encoding.
+2. **One link expression per link, always passing the specialty.** Rejected: every unnarrowed pagination URL would gain an empty `specialty=`, changing URLs the directory serves today.
+3. **Each link picks between two parameterized link expressions on a null test** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Every pagination link in `vets/vetList.html` is a link expression with parameters. Each link tests the `specialty` model attribute for null and picks the plain form or the narrowed form. `VetController` adds that attribute only when the request narrows.
+
+No pagination link splices request text into an expression.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Thymeleaf URL-encodes the specialty in every link, and no caller text reaches the expression parser.
+- An unnarrowed page keeps exactly the URLs it serves today.
+- The null test repeats across five links. Collapsing it into one always-passed parameter reintroduces the empty `specialty=`, so the repetition is load-bearing.
+- A later visible control for the specialty reuses this form rather than the preprocessing form.
+- Expression preprocessing stays in use elsewhere in the templates. Every remaining site splices an identifier, a page number, or a template-supplied field name, never free text from a caller.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+- `src/main/resources/templates/vets/vetList.html`
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vet/VetController.java`
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md — Threat Model](../system-design.md#threat-model) — the row recording this mitigation.
+- [system-design.md — Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the controller row that supplies the model attribute.
+- [Server-Side HTML Rendering with Thymeleaf](2026-07-31-server-side-rendering-with-thymeleaf.md) — the rendering choice this works within.
+- [Specialty Narrowing Runs in the Database and Stays Out of the Vet Cache](2026-08-21-uncached-database-narrowing-of-the-vet-directory.md) — the sibling decision for the same requirement.
